{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents","id":885305,"title":"Who is the god of Exigents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-08T05:29:07-07:00","id":885305,"title":"Who is the god of Exigents","content":"While responding to another thread a question hit me.<br /> <br /> Lytec, the Right Hand of Power, has perview over Celestial Exaltations and there is also a Left Hand of Power for Terrestrial exaltations. If I really cared enough to dig through the 2nd ed books to find his actual name I'd post it here.<br /> <br /> The question is. Who is charge of Exigent exalations? Does it fall under Lytecs domain or the Left Hands or is there a 3rd god who monitors there work? This is Yu-Shan we are talking about here. They aren't going to just let these exalts run around without any documentation of what they are up to just because the god who exalted them gave up their life to create them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4498-ardis","name":"Ardis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T05:38:40-07:00","id":885311,"title":"","content":"I have no idea, but I think Sol would be a good candidate. All exigents are partly fueled by him, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T05:38:47-07:00","id":885312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ardis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents#post885305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While responding to another thread a question hit me.<br /> <br /> Lytec, the Right Hand of Power, has perview over Celestial Exaltations and there is also a Left Hand of Power for Terrestrial exaltations. If I really cared enough to dig through the 2nd ed books to find his actual name I'd post it here.<br /> <br /> The question is. Who is charge of Exigent exalations? Does it fall under Lytecs domain or the Left Hands or is there a 3rd god who monitors there work? This is Yu-Shan we are talking about here. They aren't going to just let these exalts run around without any documentation of what they are up to just because the god who exalted them gave up their life to create them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would suspect that they are divided between Lytek and Parad (God of Inherited Might/the Left Hand of Power), depending on how and if their powers are passed on.<br /> So if a given Exigent reincarnates like a celestial then they are probably under his domain, while one whose powers goes to whomever is their heir/eldest son then it would be under Parads domain.<br /> Through really the god that most of them would be under the domain of their individual patron, or possibly her replacement should she have died since choosing them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/613-vegetalss4","name":"Vegetalss4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar613_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T05:54:20-07:00","id":885319,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking Vegetalss4 is probably correct here.<br /> <br /> Though, I think it could lead to some interesting lobbying for Exigents on the part of Lytec and Parad as their power ebbs and flows based on the number of Exigents that they have under their domain. It also doesn't really answer the question for those Exigents that are one shots. Their exaltation ends with them. Though it is also stated that some Exigent exalations are passed on in other esoteric ways. So, I could see an Exigent exaltation being passed on through some ritual performed by a high priest or even to the person who killed the person who had the exaltation before them. Though I suppose an argument could be made in these cases that they would fall under Lytecs domain.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4498-ardis","name":"Ardis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T06:34:36-07:00","id":885336,"title":"","content":"I'm also in favor of &quot;no god of exaltations&quot; as a thing in general, even though i have myself used Lytek and Parad both in past 2e games. Their purviews stand in a very weird place conceptually when you look hard at them, being at the same time incredibly small/restricted and weirdly abrangent. &quot;Each exalt stands under the purview of its individual patron&quot; as Vegetalss4 suggested feels more concise, elegant and less prone to pushing the ST in weird gymnastics in trying to gauge out their capacities.<br /> <br /> Not saying one cannot make them work, but personally i feel that they might work much better if they had different, but more abrangent purviews that happen to also cover/relate to their 2e concepts somewhat, like Parad being a god of inheritance/lineage/ancestry, what lets him keep tabs in the dragon-bloods and a number of lineages of spirit provenance but also a bunch of all too mortal families, high or low, for whom issues of paternity/pedigree might matter, not to mention possible nebulously deep, and quite irregular if not quite illegal, ties with a number of honored ancestors and their cults in the underworld, what could be awesome.<br /> <br /> That said i'm the first to admit Parad was much easier - and fun - to &quot;retool&quot; than Lytek, with whom i still have no ideas about what could he oversee beside the exalts, who i think can be far more properly and effectivelly kept tabs of by their own patrons, should be said. Oh, well, maybe re-reading his profile in CoCD3: Yu-shan helps...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-08-2016, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T06:56:16-07:00","id":885343,"title":"","content":"I'd say that each Exigent probably has a different relationship with their patron, but for bureaucratic purposes they're not automatically subordinates. I also don't think each god has an adendum in their portfolio that reads &quot;and all my Exigents, if any&quot;. Rather, the perpetually detached Sol is the god of the Exigence. If you have any objections regarding the process, you can take it up with him.<br /> <br /> Also, Lytek isn't the god of Celestial Exalted, he's the god of the process of Exaltation (even Terrestrial Exaltation is under his authority by virtue of hierarchy; Parad is his subordinate, not his counterpart). He probably has some duties re: Exigents as well, though of course he doesn't have much *actual* influence over Exaltation of any kind anyway. It remains to be seen how all these new Exalted we have now are going to fit into that bureaucratic structure in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 05-08-2016, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T07:30:15-07:00","id":885366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885343#post885343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Lytek isn't the god of Celestial Exalted, he's the god of the process of Exaltation (even Terrestrial Exaltation is under his authority by virtue of hierarchy; Parad is his subordinate, not his counterpart).</div> </div> </div> </div>True, what makes his purview even <b>more</b> ungainly to work with overall, imho. What exactly does he exist <b>for</b>, beside playing second fiddle to what could more properly - and dramatically - dealt with by one's own divine patron or sort of explaining (not really necessarily) the nebulous gaps in time between incarnations or what memories are remembered between them?<br /> <br /> Hmmmm, god of <b>memories</b> lost....nice, nice, that could work, interesting. Wait, what was the point? Ah, whatever, back to my notes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-08-2016, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T08:40:31-07:00","id":885396,"title":"","content":"There wouldn't <i>be</i> a god of Exigents. The god of an Exigent is its patron. There's no god of Sidereals, there's the Five Maidens. There's no God of Solars, there's the Unconquered Sun. There's no god of Lunars, there's <i>Luna.</i> The god of any given Exigent is the one that created it. If anything like Lytek <i>does</i> still exist, the one who clears Exaltations of past lives or whatever, then the Exigents, as Exalts, would fall under <i>Lytek,</i> since they are, you know, Exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:22:59-07:00","id":885419,"title":"","content":"The closest to such a position would be the Unconquered Sun, as He processes the petitions and provides the Divine Fire, but I wouldn't expect there to be an official position in the Bureau of Destiny for managing the Exigents, because the UCS already does so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:36:51-07:00","id":885428,"title":"","content":"IIRC: In 2e Lytek was responsible for handling the shards of exaltation before they went off to be claimed by the next random exaltation. He cleans them of the horrible sins and possible derangements they may have gained from traumatic experiences, blurs out anything trivial and then runs a highlighter over the epic moments from that exaltations past. He is literally the &quot;Caretaker of the Exaltation&quot; itself.<br /> <br /> I believe there was actually speculation in some of the books (this may just be my head cannon) that Lytek is <i>semi-</i><i>aware</i> of a problem with the exaltations (re: The Great Curse), but has been completely ineffectual in actually substantiating that a problem actually exists, and so is entirely unsure of his speculation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11632-ramaloke","name":"Ramaloke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:41:41-07:00","id":885431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885419#post885419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest to such a position would be the Unconquered Sun, as He processes the petitions and provides the Divine Fire, but I wouldn't expect there to be an official position in the Bureau of Destiny for managing the Exigents, because the UCS already does so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it would be in the Bureau of Heaven, Abstract Matters. Which is where Lytec actually sits. He use to be a shogun or whatever of Abstract Matters, but he got pushed out after the Usurption. As for the Unconquered Sun and doing the paperwork in second edition they gave him his own office of gods that did the paperwork for him and he just signed off on it.<br /> <br /> My original point with this post is that in Exalted Heaven creates mountains of paperwork for every gentle breeze. I just find it hard to believe that the Unconquered Sun would sign off on creating Exigents and just let them go about doing as they please without having some god watching what is going on with them. Since many gods have to give up their own existence to create an Exigent you would think that there would be some mechanism with the Divine Bureaucracy to at least generate the paperwork detailing what damage they may or may not be doing to the creation as they blow off tons of essence doing whatever they feel like doing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4498-ardis","name":"Ardis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:49:00-07:00","id":885439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramaloke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885428#post885428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC: In 2e Lytek was responsible for handling the shards of exaltation before they went off to be claimed by the next random exaltation. He cleans them of the horrible sins and possible derangements they may have gained from traumatic experiences, blurs out anything trivial and then runs a highlighter over the epic moments from that exaltations past. He is literally the &amp;quot;Caretaker of the Exaltation&amp;quot; itself.<br /> <br /> I believe there was actually speculation in some of the books (this may just be my head cannon) that Lytek is <i>semi-</i><i>aware</i> of a problem with the exaltations (re: The Great Curse), but has been completely ineffectual in actually substantiating that a problem actually exists, and so is entirely unsure of his speculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall Lytek is *acutely* aware of the Great Curse, one of maybe a handful of beings in heaven and earth who know about it. Problem is he has no idea what to do about it, and doesn't trust anyone enough to talk about it. By extension that means Nara-O probably knows, and the Maiden of Secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:51:01-07:00","id":885441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ardis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885431#post885431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it would be in the Bureau of Heaven, Abstract Matters. Which is where Lytec actually sits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooops, I misspoke. I meant &quot;Celestial Bureaucracy&quot;. Apologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:51:33-07:00","id":885442,"title":"","content":"Many gods die when empowering a Chosen through Exaltation. And to have Exigents running around causing problems without a deity to record their activities and submit monthly reports to the Harmonious Division of the Activities of Exalted would be most terrible. While you might scoff and suggest that there is no <i>need </i> to submit reports, keep in mind that without reports being submitted to them, the Harmonious Devising of the Activities of Exalted would have no reason to exist and it's gods would find themselves without a job. Most distressing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T11:38:56-07:00","id":885527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885366#post885366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, what makes his purview even <b>more</b> ungainly to work with overall, imho. What exactly does he exist <b>for</b>, beside playing second fiddle to what could more properly - and dramatically - dealt with by one's own divine patron or sort of explaining (not really necessarily) the nebulous gaps in time between incarnations or what memories are remembered between them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like any god, he is tasked with observing his domain and reporting back\u2014or intervening\u2014if something within his purview goes wrong.<br /> <br /> What could go wrong with Exaltation?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T11:53:07-07:00","id":885547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885527#post885527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What could go wrong with Exaltation?</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZnHmskwqCCQ\" data-code=\"ZnHmskwqCCQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZnHmskwqCCQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T12:22:46-07:00","id":885579,"title":"","content":"I imagine Lytek does most of the paperwork for Exigents, but there's some that go to Parad because they're more his department. There may be some unclassifiables that don't really fit either of their purviews, which is probably cause for them to throw up their hands and get a stiff drink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T12:44:15-07:00","id":885601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885366#post885366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, what makes his purview even <b>more</b> ungainly to work with overall, imho. What exactly does he exist <b>for</b>, beside playing second fiddle to what could more properly - and dramatically - dealt with by one's own divine patron or sort of explaining (not really necessarily) the nebulous gaps in time between incarnations or what memories are remembered between them?<br /> <br /> Hmmmm, god of <b>memories</b> lost....nice, nice, that could work, interesting. Wait, what was the point? Ah, whatever, back to my notes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose you could always specify that he is the god of bestowed power and thus by association also god of promotions. His demotion might also be related to the ossification of rank in Heaven and the class structure on Creation. As the bestowal of power par excellence he would also be god of Exaltations in general, Celestial in particular, and most Exigent. Parad would be his subordinate who oversees power bestowed by birth which would include both Terrestrial Exaltations, the lineages of gods and demons, and the transfer of property and social position between the generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:54:41-07:00","id":885665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885579#post885579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine Lytek does most of the paperwork for Exigents, but there's some that go to Parad because they're more his department. There may be some unclassifiables that don't really fit either of their purviews, which is probably cause for them to throw up their hands and get a stiff drink.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, for Clarity's sake, Lytek and Parad are still setting elements and they watch over the concepts of Exaltation? They haven't been rendered thematically irrelevant like the Least Gods of a particular teacup have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:15:38-07:00","id":885693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885665#post885665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, for Clarity's sake, Lytek and Parad are still setting elements and they watch over the concepts of Exaltation? They haven't been rendered thematically irrelevant like the Least Gods of a particular teacup have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I'm just imagining. That's a dev call, and if it's been made one way or the other I dunno about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:20:09-07:00","id":885700,"title":"","content":"Why would they get rid of Lytek and Parad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:39:51-07:00","id":885711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885700#post885700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they get rid of Lytek and Parad?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's their point, really? They seem to be re-emphasizing the Incarna in the Exaltation process, and de-emphasizing past lives and such. Why do you need gods of Exaltation, then? We already have gods in charge of that. They're named Sol, Luna, Mercury...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T15:36:26-07:00","id":885739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885700#post885700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they get rid of Lytek and Parad?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see an argument to cut Parad in the 'don't mention him again' sense because a lot of people interpreted his existence to mean that Lytek's purview didn't cover Dragon-Blooded anymore.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T16:09:36-07:00","id":885763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885711#post885711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's their point, really? \u2026 Why do you need gods of Exaltation, then? We already have gods in charge of that. They're named Sol, Luna, Mercury...</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you expect <i>them</i> to file paperwork like some sort of plebs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T16:53:12-07:00","id":885784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885763#post885763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you expect <i>them</i> to file paperwork like some sort of plebs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always kinda figured there wasn't paperwork related to Exalted so much as paperwork related to the actions of Exalted. So everyone files paperwork except the Incarna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T17:09:02-07:00","id":885801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885527#post885527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like any god, he is tasked with observing his domain and reporting back\u2014or intervening\u2014if something within his purview goes wrong.<br /> <br /> What could go wrong with Exaltation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what could he do that is not more appropriate for the Incarnae or some more direct agent/expy/tutelary deity to do? With Parad the subject of lineage and inheritance acutally offers a decent excuse to branch out and make him into a conveniently abrangent deity. Exaltation as a concept to have a specific overseer seems to stand at a pretty peculiar place in the matters of hierarchy, abstration and such, being at the same time ludricously specialized, what's almost a synonym of irrelevance and yet tied to some of the most influential individuals of Creation and their frequently far-reaching acts. Not to mention the whole &quot;general expy of all incarna&quot; thing that also sort of results from this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T17:35:36-07:00","id":885828,"title":"","content":"I can see the argument to reimagine Lytek for 3e.<br /> He's traditionally rooted in a very dehumanising view of Exaltation that might be worth taking the time to dismantle since he could still be interesting as a bureaucrat who has been recording the exploits of the Exalted since the First Age and probably knows any Exalt who gets to see him well enough to qualify as their unofficial biographer.<br /> <br /> It lends itself to more than &quot;no! unpack your 2e baggage! bad! baaaad!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T17:39:54-07:00","id":885830,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying we can't reimagine him - I'm just defending him from the folks saying he's useless or that they want to see him purged altogether with hateful green fire or turned into starmetal (admittedly most of that's in other threads, but still).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T18:02:19-07:00","id":885836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885830#post885830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying we can't reimagine him - I'm just defending him from the folks saying he's useless or that they want to see him purged altogether with hateful green fire or turned into starmetal (admittedly most of that's in other threads, but still).</div> </div> </div> </div>Recycling i'm certainly ok with - waste not, want not. Adapting is fine and truth be told talking with people here has already helped with polishing something for Lytek per se, who i was still having some difficulty with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T18:03:39-07:00","id":885838,"title":"","content":"I've always kind of liked Lytek as a god. Even if it is just that he does the day to day drudge work that the Incarne can't be bothered to worry about with the exaltations. Plus, without his cabinet the whole Usurption and sealing the Solar Exaltations away in the Jade Prison kind of falls apart.<br /> <br /> He works as a good intermediary for high powered characters that can get into Yu-Shan, but can't get into the Jade Pleasure Dome to speak with the Unconquered Sun directly. Though I've also had him manipulate players for his own ends. But I've also done that with Little Beam, if anyone here gets that reference.<br /> <br /> Though it would be interesting to see an Exigent of Lytek. The Chosen of Exaltations. That could be interesting.<br /> <br /> Lytek knows about the Great Curse, but only as it pertains to Solars. The problem is that he hasn't been able to find a way to fix it and he's afraid to tell the Unconquered Sun because he's afraid it will make him look incompetent at his job. It is also pointed out in the 1st edition Cult of the Illuminated book that he is extremely interested in a rogue Abyssal in their ranks as he thinks that the fact that the curse has been removed from him it might lead him to a cure for all Solars.<br /> <br /> So, I could see Lytek creating an Exigent to put in a party of Solars in an effort to find a way to either cure the Great Curse or at least study it up close and in action in active Solars. Though this does bring to mind another question that I think I'll start a new thread on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4498-ardis","name":"Ardis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T18:14:15-07:00","id":885843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885828#post885828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the argument to reimagine Lytek for 3e.<br /> He's traditionally rooted in a very dehumanising view of Exaltation that might be worth taking the time to dismantle since he could still be interesting as a bureaucrat who has been recording the exploits of the Exalted since the First Age and probably knows any Exalt who gets to see him well enough to qualify as their unofficial biographer.<br /> <br /> It lends itself to more than &quot;no! unpack your 2e baggage! bad! baaaad!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I do wonder actually how Abyssals and Infernals work now, since Exaltations are hero seeking drones anymore and are apparently granted by the notice of the Sun. I don't thing Sol now sometimes bestows black or green Solars by accident and there is no way the Primordials would let him award their Exaltations. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ardis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885838#post885838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, without his cabinet the whole Usurption and sealing the Solar Exaltations away in the Jade Prison kind of falls apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. They could have just stole the fates of heroes from the Loom of Fate such that the situation never comes up where the right people are in the right place and time to have a shot at catching the notice of the Sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T18:38:30-07:00","id":885863,"title":"","content":"I like Lytek as the God of Exaltation- not of the Exalted or of Exaltation<b>s </b>note pluralization of.<br /> A lot of the 'Lytek maintains, trims and grooms the Exalted Essences' stuff (which, to be far, was always present) had, I feel, an unexpectedly mechanisticizing (is that a word?) of the act of Exaltation; it moved away from being a miracle and become more firmly Sufficiently Advanced Magic.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of him act as the unofficial biographer of the Exalted, but that should be, like, a hobby. His *job* should be rubberstamping reports that read like 'Today, three people Exalted. They are Bob the Baker, Chompy the Lunar and Ragara Alice. Their Exaltations occured without incident.'<br /> <br /> And very occusionally, passing a report to the Sidereals of 'Today, Bob Exalted. Sort of. See, Han-Tha got his hands on an Exigent Exaltation, and it was already pretty screwed up before that, and... yeah, if you could get someone down to Rathess by Saturnday, that'd be just super.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T19:08:47-07:00","id":885875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885863#post885863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Lytek as the God of Exaltation- not of the Exalted or of Exaltation<b>s </b>note pluralization of.<br /> A lot of the 'Lytek maintains, trims and grooms the Exalted Essences' stuff (which, to be far, was always present) had, I feel, an unexpectedly mechanisticizing (is that a word?) of the act of Exaltation; it moved away from being a miracle and become more firmly Sufficiently Advanced Magic.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of him act as the unofficial biographer of the Exalted, but that should be, like, a hobby. His *job* should be rubberstamping reports that read like 'Today, three people Exalted. They are Bob the Baker, Chompy the Lunar and Ragara Alice. Their Exaltations occured without incident.'<br /> <br /> And very occusionally, passing a report to the Sidereals of 'Today, Bob Exalted. Sort of. See, Han-Tha got his hands on an Exigent Exaltation, and it was already pretty screwed up before that, and... yeah, if you could get someone down to Rathess by Saturnday, that'd be just super.'</div> </div> </div> </div>You could formalize the roll of biographer if he is in charge of the legend each exalt makes and his pruning is things like irrelevant details or the sorts of human incidents that don't contribute to the appropriate mythic archetypes.<br /> <br /> Also, I would worry about making Heaven just an emergent reflection of Creation. If the gods just produce and file reports but no one outside of BuDest can actually do things legally then Heaven is structured as the Universes way of keeping score of what is important on Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T20:04:29-07:00","id":885913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ardis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885838#post885838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, without his cabinet the whole Usurption and sealing the Solar Exaltations away in the Jade Prison kind of falls apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>All three of the Core books did just fine without mentioning it. I sure didn't question whether the JP was modeled after some other gizmo in my first foray into Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ardis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885838#post885838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I've also done that with Little Beam, if anyone here gets that reference.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://imgur.com/XS5LK\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T22:42:06-07:00","id":885971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ardis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885838#post885838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, without his cabinet the whole Usurption and sealing the Solar Exaltations away in the Jade Prison kind of falls apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how. The Sidereals don't have to loot some literal cabinet for Exaltations. They can have just done some kind of intense Sorcerous Working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T23:41:35-07:00","id":885984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885843#post885843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do wonder actually how Abyssals and Infernals work now, since Exaltations are hero seeking drones anymore and are apparently granted by the notice of the Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou know that even in Second Edition, Abyssal and Infernal Exaltation were granted by the direct will and choice of the Deathlords and Yozis respectively?<br /> <br /> The significance of the &quot;Exaltation as self-directed thing&quot; was retained purely in a rationale for why those entities didn't have complete latitude in who they could choose, and what would happen if their control mechanisms were broken.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T23:56:33-07:00","id":885990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=885984#post885984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bYou know that even in Second Edition, Abyssal and Infernal Exaltation were granted by the direct will and choice of the Deathlords and Yozis respectively?<br /> <br /> The significance of the &quot;Exaltation as self-directed thing&quot; was retained purely in a rationale for why those entities didn't have complete latitude in who they could choose, and what would happen if their control mechanisms were broken.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The omission of a &quot;n't&quot; aside, I have been imagining Exaltations in 3E as being more like relationships with the patron than artifact N/A glowing motes. It seems a lot harder to pervert the miracle of the Sun's noticing and falling in love with someone than it is to slap some yozi essence on a magic ball and have at it. I suppose this will just invite another round (I don't expect them from you) of accusations that I fail to understand the concept of something intangible being affected by other things, but perhaps it has more to do with no longer thinking of Exaltations as having an existence beyond the patron's choice. (Such that there is no Cabinet where Exaltations hang out between mortals taking second breath, they don't exist until Luna, or the Maidens, or whomever sees someone and their nature moves them to make champions of them at which point suddenly there is an Exalt and the Exaltation is the event.)<br /> <br /> Though I don't seem to recall the Yozi having much say in the matter since they literally had to stuff the Exaltation into a demon who went around following the things own guidance system and then did the bargaining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 05-09-2016, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T01:00:51-07:00","id":886017,"title":"","content":"I don't have a problem with exaltations as things that exist because there are already abstract things that exist, like souls, or the breath of a fish and sound of a cat's footfall that Ms. Solar Artificer worked into an artifact chain to bind an unkillable behemoth last Marsday, or the prayers that fill the quintessence fountains. That some gods can manipulate them doesn't mean they are concrete objects that just anyone can see and pick up and tinker with a screwdriver, it means that the gods and Primordials have numinous and miraculous abilities and Heaven and Hell are miraculous places of wonders that would strain human perception, let alone comprehension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T03:00:36-07:00","id":886061,"title":"","content":"This is what I mean when I say dehumanising. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted: the Sidereals</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Although he considers the Dragon-Blooded little more than interesting pets he sees all Celestial Exalted as somewhere between his children and his art projects. However, he is extremely patronising and feels he is far wiser than any of his creations. He touches Celestial Exalted without their permission and comments on facets of their personalities and powers as if he were discussing a work of art.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T08:14:23-07:00","id":886277,"title":"","content":"Uh... ew ... is this along the lines of all gods being jerks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2016, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:38:29-07:00","id":886345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886277#post886277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh... ew ... is this along the lines of all gods being jerks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it was something published in a 2e book for certain - not the same book from &quot;Are all gods jerks?&quot; (that said, the books actually tried to say the opposite of the meaning it took for most of the fanbase, but i'll concede it could have been better thought out/written), though i had myself to check to be actually certain.<br /> <br /> Doesn't make Lytek a jerk per se i guess, but the idea that the sense of identity of almost all celestial exalts might be the aesthetic works of art/xanatos gambits of some patronizing god, no matter how supposedly innocuous benign, does leave a very sour aftertaste one can certainly do without.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-09-2016, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:47:09-07:00","id":886357,"title":"","content":"Lioness's quote come from Ex1 though, Exalted: Splat is Ex1 version of Ex2's MoEP: Splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:49:51-07:00","id":886360,"title":"","content":"Yes, that's from Lytek's original 1e appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:56:24-07:00","id":886366,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Lytek is the creepy uncle you don't want to be left alone with.<br /> <br /> I prefer Lytek to be a Celestial Exalt Fanboy who is pissed that one group of Celestial Exalts beat him up and killed off another group of Celestial Exalts.<br /> <br /> There is no rage like fanboy rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-09-2016, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:02:33-07:00","id":886374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886366#post886366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Lytek is the creepy uncle you don't want to be left alone with.<br /> <br /> I prefer Lytek to be a Celestial Exalt Fanboy who is pissed that one group of Celestial Exalts beat him up and killed off part of his another group of Celestial Exalts.<br /> <br /> There is no rage like fanboy rage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &gt;.&gt;<br /> &lt;.&lt;<br /> <b>stolen</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:05:32-07:00","id":886380,"title":"","content":"I imagine that Lytek would come across as a slightly more handsome version of Ollivander from Harry Potter, right down to having a certain uncomfortably reverent tone when discussing certain Exalted engaged in troubling activities.<br /> <br /> Ollivander wasn't very touchy as I recall, beyond taking measurements (even if he kind of leaped straight into that), but I'd see something equivalent in his tendency to recite the details of people's wands whenever meeting or mentioning them, which seems about equivalent given attitudes to wands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lytek is the creepy uncle you don't want to be left alone with.</div> </div> </div> </div>At one extreme. At another, he's that kind of pushy aunt who invades personal space, pinches cheeks, and asks very probing personal questions at the drop of a hat, with the occasional comment speculating if you're eating enough.<br /> <br /> .... Why are these things gendered?!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:18:24-07:00","id":886389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886374#post886374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &gt;.&gt;<br /> &lt;.&lt;<br /> <b>stolen</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why do you keep stealing my shit!? :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886380#post886380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that Lytek would come across as a slightly more handsome version of Ollivander from Harry Potter, right down to having a certain uncomfortably reverent tone when discussing certain Exalted engaged in troubling activities.<br /> <br /> Ollivander wasn't very touchy as I recall, beyond taking measurements (even if he kind of leaped straight into that), but I'd see something equivalent in his tendency to recite the details of people's wands whenever meeting or mentioning them, which seems about equivalent given attitudes to wands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886380#post886380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At one extreme. At another, he's that kind of pushy aunt who invades personal space, pinches cheeks, and asks very probing personal questions at the drop of a hat, with the occasional comment speculating if you're eating enough.<br /> <br /> .... Why are these things gendered?!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know.... To be honest, I don't want to be left alone with Auntie Lytek any more than Uncle Lytek.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:35:34-07:00","id":886410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886357#post886357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lioness's quote come from Ex1 though, Exalted: Splat is Ex1 version of Ex2's MoEP: Splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the correction, must admit i completely forgot Lytek was actually mentioned in 1e's Exalted: Sidereals, as i guess it was the source of most of the stuff we know about the celestial gods and Yu-shan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886380#post886380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that Lytek would come across as a slightly more handsome version of Ollivander from Harry Potter, right down to having a certain uncomfortably reverent tone when discussing certain Exalted engaged in troubling activities.<br /> <br /> Ollivander wasn't very touchy as I recall, beyond taking measurements (even if he kind of leaped straight into that), but I'd see something equivalent in his tendency to recite the details of people's wands whenever meeting or mentioning them, which seems about equivalent given attitudes to wands.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a valid comparison, but even without the touchiness it does bother me considerable due to the whole &quot;acessing, picking and pruning&quot; an exalt's memories of its past lives, something a little too close to selective brainwashing/Dominate abuse in Masquerade/Requiem for my confort...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886380#post886380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At one extreme. At another, he's that kind of pushy aunt who invades personal space, pinches cheeks, and asks very probing personal questions at the drop of a hat, with the occasional comment speculating if you're eating enough.<br /> <br /> .... Why are these things gendered?!</div> </div> </div> </div>As i mentioned in another topic, the selective <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/StalkingIsFunnyIfItIsFemaleAfterMale\" target=\"_blank\">lenses</a> of certain <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DoubleStandardAbuseFemaleOnMale\" target=\"_blank\">convenient tropes</a>, mostly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-09-2016, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:38:31-07:00","id":886416,"title":"","content":"Now that I think of it, maybe also some of the Bajoran spiritual practice of grasping people's ears firmly in order to get a sense of their soul, from Star Trek: Deep Space Nine.<br /> <br /> As I recall, even reasonable and sympathetic characters never asked permission to do this, which would lead me to think it's something in the area of a highly intimate greeting rather then an intrusion from their perspective, even if it sometimes makes characters unfamiliar with the practice uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> In Lytek's case, it might be him placing his palm on the crown of your head, or several of his fingers on the spot where your Caste mark appears, at which he'll typically smile knowingly and mysteriously.<br /> <br /> If it's not apparent, I quite like the description of Lytek touching people. I say that as somebody who is quite averse to being touched by basically anybody in real life (although for the literally one person who I can stand to do so, I quite enjoy physical affection, not least because he's generally very withholding with it, so... not sure what's going on there).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:42:06-07:00","id":886422,"title":"","content":"Oops, I missed an entire page of replies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886360#post886360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that's from Lytek's original 1e appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the basic concept of Lytek, but had developed my own headcanon image of him as somebody whose work with exaltations was a sacred, indescribable, mystical art form, who regarded exaltations as wondrous works of art and respected Exalted as high-status people in their own right. I'd prefer that most gods view Exalted as somebody to respect.<br /> <br /> Was 1E also the edition in which Celestial gods in general despise Sidereals, and view Dragon-Bloods as non-people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2016, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:47:07-07:00","id":886430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886422#post886422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oops, I missed an entire page of replies.<br /> <br /> I like the basic concept of Lytek, but would prefer that most gods view Exalted as somebody to respect.<br /> Was 1E also the edition in which Celestial gods in general despise Sidereals, and view Dragon-Bloods as non-people?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I recall that was much more a 2E thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:52:15-07:00","id":886438,"title":"","content":"It's a 2e thing but as you can see from bits like that it's not something that a 2e writer pulled out their ass.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:56:25-07:00","id":886447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886438#post886438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a 2e thing but as you can see from bits like that it's not something that a 2e writer pulled out their ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, definitely. The 1e Sidereals book has some fairly demeaning things about the place of Dragonblooded relative to Celestial Exalted, especially Solars, while in Heaven. Likewise, there's definitely bits about some Gods still carrying a grudge because of the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> CoCD:Yu-shan then emphasized both of these ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:57:26-07:00","id":886449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886389#post886389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why do you keep stealing my shit!? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually just a very advanced Markov generator, and must steal content from others to appear even vaguely original.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:00:34-07:00","id":886452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886449#post886449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually just a very advanced Markov generator, and must steal content from others to appear even vaguely original.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ha! Jokes on you! I am also a very advance Markov generator! <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Steal-Like-Artist-Things-Creative-ebook/dp/B0074QGGK6?ie=UTF8&amp;btkr=1&amp;ref_=dp-kindle-redirect\" target=\"_blank\">You are stealing from a thief! </a> :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:02:32-07:00","id":886455,"title":"","content":"Iiiiii like the stuff about Celestial gods being snooty with Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> I mean, Celestial gods are apparently snooty with the Elemental Dragons. Probably mostly in private, and from very far away.<br /> <br /> I read the latter as a suggestion that the snootiness of Celestial gods is not something to take very seriously, past how some will oppress or murder you over it if they can.<br /> <br /> Why, as I recall, they're even a bit snooty with Celestial Exalted who aren't Sidereals.<br /> <br /> I like the descriptions of writing Heaven in terms of the gods being highly respectful towards Sidereals now, but I would be interested if this came across as not entirely something to be comfortable with. Like being in with the popular kids, who sincerely like and respect you, at the same time as they deride the nerdier kids who are also your friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:07:36-07:00","id":886460,"title":"","content":"I play it off as the Celestial Gods are snooty about people from Creation. It's not that the Dragonblooded is Dragonblooded. It's because they talk like a bumpkin and don't know that you wash you fingers between each course of the meal. Even a Celestial Exalt raised in Creation will get the same treatment.<br /> <br /> Eclipses and other Solars got away with a lot thanks to Mastery of Small Manners. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I should add that not EVERY Celestial God is an arrogant bastard. Some are rather nice to people from Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-09-2016, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:11:06-07:00","id":886463,"title":"","content":"As with many potentially problematic ideas, no single expression of an idea (Celestial Gods demeaning Dragonblooded, a strained relationship between Sidereals and the Gods) is neccesarily bad- it's the impression from the aggregate collection of problematic ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:16:47-07:00","id":886474,"title":"","content":"I'm cool with Celestial gods being snooty and chauvinistic in general, and I assume some would be unhappy with how the Second Age has turned out, but not that they would regard Exalted as mere pets or toys. There's a difference between having an audience with a dignitary of a foreign nation who is powerful, and you need to show respect and acknowledge her importance, but at the same time your mannerisms and use of your native customs make it clear that you think you're better than her, versus ... groping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2016, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:27:38-07:00","id":886494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886455#post886455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iiiiii like the stuff about Celestial gods being snooty with Dragon Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I question whose benefit stuff like that is for because most Dragon-Blooded PCs will never go anywhere near Yu-Shan and the exceptions tend to be exceptional enough that these preconceptions just dirty the water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:58:21-07:00","id":886523,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the attitude of gods toward other people might be broadly analogous to people in rich and insular 1st world countries to those in third world countries from which they extract resources and cheap labor. They are aware they exist, they derive personal benefit from a few of them, but they don't consider them as people in the same sense they do their peers or the population of their own place of residence. So a dragon blooded showing up is like some warlord who thinks she is rich and important barging into your house and making demands. Solars are either foreign nobility that gains prestige from the ancient and respected nation they are from OR representatives of states you can respect but still think are not your nation's equal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T12:02:08-07:00","id":886528,"title":"","content":"I wonder what kind of treatment the Scarlet Empress would get in Yu-Shan, and how it might be different than the treatment received by a much less famous DB in her entourage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T16:18:01-07:00","id":887594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886528#post886528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what kind of treatment the Scarlet Empress would get in Yu-Shan, and how it might be different than the treatment received by a much less famous DB in her entourage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like big, bad, third world country ruler in official or informal visit and young distant nephew or cousin nobody heard about tagging along, possibly. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Even without going with exthalion's comparison for reference, she's a dragon-blooded that has managed to directly rule a whole direction and influence a pretty large chunk of Creation for more than 3/4 of a millenium, beside doing occasional displays of power that one might compare to Sapphire Circle Sorcery, so i would guess that guarded respect at least matching that given to a celestial exalt should be the norm in her case.<br /> In the case of your &quot;generic dragon-blood&quot;, if the might table serves as any indicator, one would expect them to be roughly on par or slightly more puisant than spirits of comparable Essence, so, something like elementals or &quot;minor&quot; gods in the Ess2-4 range, unless you really screwed up with Fate and got to be face-to-face with Cathak Cainan, Tepet Arada or Mnemon. My total @$$pull guesstimations anyway, take it all with a bit of salt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T16:55:01-07:00","id":887630,"title":"","content":"She is legitimately an actual Celestial Circle Sorcerer, as long as she keeps the Mantle of Brigid on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:21:57-07:00","id":887785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=887630#post887630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She is legitimately an actual Celestial Circle Sorcerer, as long as she keeps the Mantle of Brigid on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supposing it's the <b>real</b> Mantle of Brigid and not a piece of misdirection to trick antagonists into ignoring other sources of occult power she might access, like maybe merging with a lesser elemental dragon versed in the arts of the Sapphire Circle, for example. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T16:57:15-07:00","id":891447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885305-who-is-the-god-of-exigents?p=886357#post886357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lioness's quote come from Ex1 though, Exalted: Splat is Ex1 version of Ex2's MoEP: Splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, many things from 1st ed. got reprinted in 2nd. Ed. 3rd. Ed seems to do a little bit better at re-writting or adding new stuff. Rather than whole sale copying word for word to a new book.<br /> <br /> There are definitely things in the core book for 3rd ed though that you could easily find in 1st ed. One example would be the information on the Great Houses of the Realm.","signature":"","edite